From b333abc3b30707a67e2df846e1996d58a847a828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HSS Mundur Redesign <redesign@example.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:04:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign UI and make it smooth on every device

Design
- New design system (app/globals.css): warm paper + deep-teal palette with
  lamp-gold accents, Fraunces / Figtree type, fluid type scale, arched hero
  photo, bento gallery, timeline and "at a glance" panel on About.
- One <h1> per page, real <main>, skip link, visible focus states,
  aria-current on nav, semantic lists/figures.
- New favicon (app/icon.svg) and per-page title template.

Performance / smoothness
- Optimised photos: 6000x4000 originals (~9 MB on the home page) replaced by
  responsive WebP srcsets (5-77 KB each); lazy-loaded below the fold, hero
  image is eager + high priority. scripts/optimize-images.py regenerates them.
- Removed Font Awesome (~1 MB) in favour of a small inline-SVG icon set.
- Removed the loader, film grain, particle canvas, custom cursor, tilt,
  magnetic buttons, glitch text and page wipe. Remaining motion is
  transform/opacity only, one rAF-throttled scroll listener, IntersectionObserver
  reveal, and honours prefers-reduced-motion.
- Home page is now a server component; only Header, Counter and SiteEffects
  ship client JS.

All devices
- Mobile-first layout tested from 320px to 1440px with no horizontal overflow.
- Full-screen mobile menu with scroll lock, Esc to close, 48px touch targets.
- dvh + safe-area insets (notches), viewport-fit=cover, hover effects gated
  behind (hover: hover), Little Kites iframe only embedded on wide screens.

Content is unchanged. Social links with no URL are hidden until filled in
via lib/site.js (they were dead "#" links).
